section: rts
synopsis: Update RTS flag handling: It now respects user set -n values, allows resetting of more settings to defaults and gives more accurate bounds in errors.
description:
  Using 0 as argument to any of these flags now resets the flags setting to default:

    - ``-n0`` disables nursery chunking.
    - ``-K0`` (or a bare ``-K``) removes the stack size limit.
    - ``-M0`` removes the heap size limit.
    - ``-H0`` resets the suggested heap size, including the nursery scaling set by ``-H``.
    - ``-AL0`` makes the large object allocation limit follow ``-A`` again.

  A nursery chunk size (``-n``) larger than the allocation area (``-A``) now prints a
  warning and disables nursery chunking. Previously every nursery was enlarged to the chunk size.

  The number of generations (``-G``) is now limited to 64.
